Current wasmtime-wasi-http implementation assumes and only uses HTTP/1.1:

https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/d943d57e78950da21dd430e0847f3b8fd0ade073/crates/wasi-http/src/types.rs#L375-L448

One example of this is unconditional inclusion on the `Host` header:

https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/d943d57e78950da21dd430e0847f3b8fd0ade073/crates/wasi-http/src/http_impl.rs#L71

Some servers (e.g., `google-analytics.com`) seem to prohibit `Host` headers in HTTP/2.

Only use HTTP/1.1 for most compatibility in outgoing connections for now.

See also https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7540#section-8.1.2.3

This PRs also ensures we now use the request options, e.g. connection timeout

