Interestingly, forcing 1.1 with `hyper-util` did not work, so instead we just use `hyper` directly (just like wasmtime) and implement our own connection pool per-link (lacking from wasmtime).
We should investigate ways to use http 2, if supported to talk to the remotes as a next step, but 1.1 should be good enough for now.

The last commit includes a fix to the datepicker, in it not changing when the value it is bound to changes. This issue can be tested with the following 

Angular only
```ts
  someDate = "2024-06-12";

  resetDate() {
    this.someDate = "2026-02-13";
  }

  onDateChange(e: Event) {
    this.someDate = (e as CustomEvent).detail.value;
  }


```

